    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/875/cw/en-us/job/503918/senior-pricing-manager": {
      "title": "Senior Pricing Manager",
      "description": "Senior Pricing Manager Apply now Job No: 503918 Work Type: Staff Full Time (1500 hours or greater) Location: Dayton, OH Category: Research Institute Staff Department: Research Business Serv - 250200 Pay Grade: P3/P4 - Exempt Advertised: October 02, 2026 Applications close: Position Summary: Drive Competitive Pricing. Mitigate Risk. Deliver Results. UDRI invites qualified applicants to apply for our Senior Pricing Manager opening! The Senior Pricing Manager is responsible for developing pricing and cost estimates for large, complex, strategic procurements, performing detailed costs analysis, creating basis of estimates, and developing cost volumes. This position will collaborate with technical researchers, program managers, proposal teams, and Institute leaders to evaluate the competitive landscape, mitigate financial risk, and develop sound pricing strategies. The Senior Pricing Manager will analyze industry trends, resources costs, and the competitive landscape to conduct thorough analysis, identifying areas of opportunities and risk mitigation strategies. This position will provide estimating and pricing guidance and mentorship to support team performance and successful program execution. The Senior Pricing Manager will monitor pricing performance for competitiveness and business performance and escalate potential issues and areas of risk. This position will support internal and external audits, proposal audit file maintenance, and play a significant role in the estimating system audit. This position will work in collaboration with the Contracts and Grants Office to manage all pricing templates to ensure ease of use, compliance, and effectiveness. Minimum Qualifications: P3 Minimum Requirements: • Bachelor's degree plus a minimum of six years of experience OR a master’s degree plus a minimum of five years of experience is required • Three years of experience pricing cost plus fixed fee, firm fixed price, and time and materials contracts for the federal government • Experience pricing research and development efforts • Effective written and verbal communication skills • Experience with all aspects of price and cost proposal preparation, including business risks, pricing strategies, compliance and estimating practices for the US government • Experience with developing or delivering price strategy presentations or analyses to executives and key decision makers • Extensive data analytical skills, including metrics, cost estimates, profitability, and risk • Experience developing Basis of Estimates (BOE) • Ability to effectively collaborate cross-functionally within a matrixed environment and diverse constituents, including with senior executives, business development, contracts, procurement, finance, and other key stakeholders • Advanced experience with Microsoft Excel and intermediate experience with Microsoft Word • Due to requirements of our research contracts with the U.S. federal government, candidates for this position must be a U.S. Citizen P4 Minimum Requirements: A P4 must meet all P3 minimum qualifications in addition to the qualifications listed below: • Bachelor's degree plus a minimum of ten years of experience; OR a master’s plus a minimum of nine years of experience is required • Five years of experience with all aspects of price and cost proposal preparation, including business risks, pricing strategies, compliance and estimating practices for the US government Preferred Qualifications: While not everyone may possess all of the preferred qualifications, the ideal candidate will bring many of the following: • Experience pricing cost plus fixed fee, firm fixed price, and time and materials contracts with contract values over $100M for the federal government • Expert skills in analysis tools such as Alteryx, Tableau, Power BI, or comparable tools • Experience with complex software pricing tools • Experience with ERI, BLS, or other salary survey tools • Audit experience • Active security clearance Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply please submit a cover letter addressing each minimum qualification and any applicable preferred qualifications that you meet. Closing Statement: Informed by its Catholic and Marianist mission, the University is committed to the dignity of every human being. Informed by this commitment, we seek to increase diversity in all of its forms, achieve fair outcomes, and model inclusion across our campus community. The University is committed to policies of affirmative action designed to increase the employment opportunities of individuals with disabilities and protected veterans in compliance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act of 1973. Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/875/cw/en-us/job/503916/energetic-materials-processing-technician-pressing-operations": {
      "title": "Energetic Materials Processing Technician - Pressing Operations",
      "description": "Energetic Materials Processing Technician - Pressing Operations Apply now Job No: 503916 Work Type: Staff Full Time (1500 hours or greater) Location: Eglin AFB, FL Category: Research Institute Staff Department: Energetic Materials - 250515 Pay Grade: T2 - Non Exempt Advertised: September 30, 2026 Applications close: Position Summary: UDRI is seeking a skilled and detail-oriented Energetic Materials Processing Specialist to support Pressing Operations at the High Explosive Research and Development (HERD) Facility located within the Air Force Research Laboratory (AFRL) Air Warfare Directorate at Eglin Air Force Base, Florida. This role plays an important operational and technical part in supporting the Department of the Air Force’s cutting-edge Research, Development, Test, and Evaluation (RDT&E) programs. The specialist will execute advanced pressing and consolidation operations for energetic materials and components using precision electro-mechanical and servo-hydraulic pressing systems. The candidate will work closely alongside research scientists, test engineers, and other technical specialists to advance the Air Warfare Directorate’s objectives and capabilities. Key Duties & Core Responsibilities: A. Energetic Materials Pressing & Consolidation Pressing Operations: Set up, operate, and control precision electro-mechanical and servo-hydraulic pressing systems to consolidate energetic materials with tight tolerances and specifications. Process Optimization: Monitor and control pressing variables (e.g., dwell time, compaction force, displacement rates, temperature profiles) to achieve targeted material densities and structural properties. Equipment Management: Maintain, inspect, and clean precision pressing systems, specialized die sets, pressing fixtures, and safety systems. B. Precision Metrology & Characterization Metrology: Inspect consolidated energetic samples utilizing precision balances, calipers, micrometers, and optical systems. Density Measurements: Determine sample density and porosity via gas/air pycnometry, geometric calculations, and immersion density methods. Quality Assurance: Ensure all energetic material samples adhere to engineering drawings, technical specifications, and safety tolerances. C. Data Management, Documentation & Reporting Data Collection: Accurately record, track, and archive process parameters, metrology data, and operational logs with attention to detail. Technical Communication: Effectively communicate results, observations, and opportunities for improvement to research engineers and program managers. D. Safety, Explosives Accountability & Facility Management Explosive Safety Compliance: Enforce and comply with all DoW, USAF, and AFRL safety standards, standard operating procedures (SOPs), and explosive safety guidelines. Materials Accountability: Maintain strict inventory control, documentation, and safe storage protocols for all energetic materials. Maintenance & Troubleshooting: Perform scheduled maintenance, diagnostics, and minor repairs on hydraulic, electrical, and pneumatic systems associated with pressing and laboratory equipment. Minimum Qualifications: -Associate Degree in Engineering Technology, Mechanical Technology, Materials Science, or a related technical field plus one (1) year of experience in a hands-on technical role. Work experience with energetic materials is preferable but not required. OR High School Diploma / GED plus a minimum of three (3) years of experience working in a laboratory or test environment with explosives, propellants, or other energetic materials. Other closely related work experience may be considered. -Competency with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, Teams) for work planning, technical communication, and data archival. -Due to the requirements of our research contracts with the U.S. federal government, candidates for this position must be a U.S. citizen. -Ability to obtain/maintain U.S. DoD SECRET security clearance. Preferred Qualifications: While not everyone may possess all of the preferred qualifications, the ideal candidate will bring many of the following: -Education: Bachelor of Science Degree in Engineering Technology, or closely related technical field. -Security Clearance: Possess an active Secret security clearance at the time of hire. -Hands-on experience working in energetic materials formulation, processing, pressing, handling, or testing. -Experience operating MTS, Instron, or similar servo-hydraulic and/or electro-mechanical load frames. -Formal training in explosive safety, hazardous materials handling, and munitions management. -Demonstrated mechanical and electronic troubleshooting skills with hydraulic systems and laboratory diagnostic equipment. -Attention to Detail: Executing sensitive and hazardous explosive consolidation protocols and recording metrology data where precision is essential. -Mathematical & Computational Aptitude: Ability to execute applied mathematical calculations, unit conversions, density equations, and statistical process measurements. -Problem Solving & Troubleshooting: Ability to diagnose mechanical, electrical, and procedural anomalies during consolidation and test cycles. -Safety Mindset: Uncompromising commitment to laboratory safety, personal protective equipment (PPE) requirements, and hazardous materials management. -Teamwork & Communication: Strong interpersonal and written communication skills to effectively collaborate with multidisciplinary research teams across AFRL, DoD, industrial partners, and national laboratories. Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply please submit a cover letter addressing each minimum qualification and any applicable preferred qualifications that you meet. Closing Statement: Informed by its Catholic and Marianist mission, the University is committed to the dignity of every human being. Informed by this commitment, we seek to increase diversity in all of its forms, achieve fair outcomes, and model inclusion across our campus community. The University is committed to policies of affirmative action designed to increase the employment opportunities of individuals with disabilities and protected veterans in compliance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act of 1973. Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/875/cw/en-us/job/503767/nutrition-assistant": {
      "title": "Nutrition Assistant",
      "description": "Nutrition Assistant Apply now Job No: 503767 Work Type: Staff Full Time (1500 hours or greater) Location: Dayton, OH Category: University Staff Department: SEHS Bombeck Family Learning Cntr - 210300 Pay Grade: 2 - Non Exempt Advertised: September 30, 2026 Applications close: Position Summary: Join our team as a Nutrition Assistant and help provide healthy meals that fuel children's growth, learning, and success every day! We invite qualified applicants to apply for our Nutrition Assistant opening within the Bombeck Center. This is a full time benefit eligible position that offers health, dental and vision insurance, retirement, disability, tuition assistance for you and your dependents, vacation/sick accrual and holiday pay. The Nutrition Assistant is responsible for supporting the Nutrition Specialist to prepare and disperse nutritious meals for the children, ages 5 weeks to 6 years, who attend the Bombeck Center. This also includes abiding by the Child and Adult Care Food Program (CACFP) and ODJFS licensing food safety requirements. This position will work with the Nutrition Specialist to maintain a clean and organized kitchen, storage area and assists with daily center laundry needs. The Bombeck Family Learning Center strives to provide the very best care and educational experiences for infants, toddlers and preschoolers ages 6 weeks to 5 years old by working in partnership with families as the children grow and develop. The Center is affiliated with the University of Dayton School of Education and Health Sciences. The Bombeck Family Learning Center is accredited by the National Association for the Education of Young Children (NAEYC) and holds a 5-star rating from the State of Ohio's Step Up to Quality rating system. Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent Ability to organize and efficiently prepare food, maintain kitchen and do laundry Maintain a positive working relationship with other staff members Preferred Qualifications: While not everyone may possess all of the preferred qualifications, the ideal candidate will bring many of the following: 1 year experience as a Nutrition Assistant or cook Knowledge of nutritional requirements for children 6 weeks through 6 years Knowledge of CACFP Program Effective written and verbal communication skills Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply please submit a cover letter addressing each minimum qualification and any applicable preferred qualifications that you meet. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. The University does not provide work visa sponsorship for this position. Closing Statement: Informed by its Catholic and Marianist mission, the University is committed to the dignity of every human being. Informed by this commitment, we seek to increase diversity in all of its forms, achieve fair outcomes, and model inclusion across our campus community. The University is committed to policies of affirmative action designed to increase the employment opportunities of individuals with disabilities and protected veterans in compliance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act of 1973. Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/875/cw/en-us/job/503906/assistant-dean-and-executive-director-of-enrollment-management-and-marketing": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean and Executive Director of Enrollment Management and Marketing",
      "description": "Assistant Dean and Executive Director of Enrollment Management and Marketing Apply now Job No: 503906 Work Type: Staff Full Time (1500 hours or greater) Location: Dayton, OH Category: University Staff Department: SoL Enrollment Mgmt - 230350 Pay Grade: D - Exempt Advertised: September 28, 2026 Applications close: Position Summary: University of Dayton School of Law (UDSL) invites applications and nominations for the position of Assistant Dean and Executive Director of Enrollment Management and Marketing. Reporting directly to the Dean, this senior administrative leader provides strategic direction for enrollment management, admissions, recruitment, and marketing for the School of Law’s J.D. and residential LL.M. programs, including traditional in-person and online/hybrid offerings. The Assistant Dean is a member of the School of Law leadership team and partners with faculty, staff, students, alumni, and University colleagues to build a strong and diverse applicant pool, support enrollment goals, strengthen the student experience from prospect through matriculation, and advance the School of Law’s mission and brand. Essential Responsibilities Strategic Enrollment Management and Recruitment • Develop and execute a comprehensive, data-informed enrollment management and recruitment strategy aligned with UDSL enrollment goals for class size, academic credentials, diversity, and net tuition revenue. • Work with the Dean to set annual recruitment priorities, enrollment targets, and timelines. • Set annual conversion strategies for each program and stage of the enrollment funnel, from prospect through matriculation. • Forecast enrollment, applicant volume, yield, credentials, and other key indicators; translate analysis into recommendations and timely decisions for the Dean and leadership team. • Identify emerging markets, prospective student populations, partnerships, and program opportunities that support sustainable enrollment. • Designing, coordinating and participating in recruitment and conversion events on campus, online, and at regional and national locations. • Build and maintain effective relationships with pre-law advisors, undergraduate institutions, professional organizations, prospective students, alumni, and other enrollment partners. • Develop distinct strategies that reflect the similarities and differences among traditional in-person, online/hybrid, and other law school programs. Admissions Operations and Compliance • Lead the administration of the admissions process, including application review, decision-making, communications, scholarship notifications, event invitations, and onboarding. • Advise and coordinate the Faculty Admissions Committee in consultation with the Dean. • Establish efficient, consistent, and student-centered application processing procedures; ensure staff are trained to use the admissions database, CRM, and related technologies. • Collaborate with Financial Aid and other University offices to support compliance with federal and state regulations, LSAC requirements, ABA standards, and University and School of Law policies. • Prepare accurate statistical and narrative reports for the Dean, the Director of Budgets and Operations, ABA and other accreditors, LSAC, and other authorized partners. • Support the enrollment and onboarding experience by coordinating orientation-related activities and other Law School leaders to facilitate the transition from admitted student to enrolled student. Marketing, Communications, and Brand Management • Partner with the Director of Communications and Marketing to develop and implement integrated recruitment marketing plans across print, web, email, social media, paid search, digital advertising, and other appropriate channels. • Oversee the development and timely distribution of accurate, compelling, and audience-appropriate recruitment materials and communications. • Ensure admissions-related website content is current, accessible, easy to navigate, and consistent with UDSL and University of Dayton brand standards; coordinate website updates with the appropriate University partners. • Use market research, audience insights, and campaign performance data to refine messaging, channel strategy, and return on investment. • Represent UDSL at recruitment events and communicate effectively with prospective students, families, pre-law advisors, undergraduate partners, and other influencers. People, Budget, and Cross-Campus Leadership • Lead, supervise, and develop the Admissions team, including hiring, training, goal setting, performance management, and evaluation. • Foster a collaborative, inclusive, accountable, and student-centered team culture consistent with the University’s Catholic and Marianist values. • Develop and manage the enrollment management and communications budget in collaboration with the Dean and Director of Budgets and Operations; allocate resources strategically and demonstrate responsible return on investment. • Collaborate with faculty, staff, students, alumni, and University offices to sustain recruitment, conversion, retention, and student success initiatives. • Collaborate with the Dean and Director of Budgets and Operations to develop and administer scholarship allocation strategies that are equitable, effective, and aligned with enrollment goals. • Use emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence, responsibly and ethically to improve enrollment operations, communications, analytics, and service to prospective students. • Perform other duties as assigned by the Dean. Minimum Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree. • At least five years of progressively responsible experience in enrollment management, admissions, recruitment, marketing, communications, advertising, public relations, or a related field; supervisory experience required. • Success developing and executing recruitment, marketing, communications, and social media strategies. • Knowledge of current trends and developments in graduate, professional, or undergraduate enrollment management and admissions. • Experience using enrollment data, market research, metrics, and analytics to guide strategy and evaluate outcomes. • Experience with admissions databases, LSAC systems, customer relationship management (CRM) platforms, and digital communications tools. • Experience leading and developing a team, managing competing priorities, and working effectively in a fast-paced environment. • Strong verbal, written, interpersonal, presentation, and problem-solving skills. • Knowledge of current and emerging technology (including AI) and its application to enrollment management. • Ability to build productive relationships with diverse constituencies, including faculty, staff, students, alumni, advisors, and external partners. • Experience developing scholarship strategy in line with institutional enrollment goals. • Working knowledge of Microsoft Office or Microsoft 365, databases, web-based research, online advertising, paid search, and search engine optimization. • Commitment to inclusive excellence and the ability to work respectfully and effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds. • Valid driver’s license with low risk driving record. Preferred Qualifications: While not everyone may possess all of the preferred qualifications, the ideal candidate will bring many of the following: • J.D. or master’s degree in higher education administration, counseling, student personnel, or similar strongly preferred. • Experience managing enrollment or admissions for a law school, graduate school, or other professional school. • Experience with financial aid concepts, scholarship strategy, and enrollment revenue management. • Demonstrated experience with project management principles, practices, tools, and techniques. • Experience with web content management, digital analytics, paid search marketing, search engine optimization, and significant website or marketing projects. • Experience developing recruitment strategies for online, hybrid, and in-person programs. • Demonstrated experience working with emerging technologies, including various forms of AI as it pertains to enrollment management. • Willingness to leverage and lead an experienced team. • Knowledge of ABA, LSAC, and law school admissions and accreditation environments. • Demonstrated knowledge and appreciation of Catholic Marianist values, and to the University of Dayton’s Mission on inclusive excellence. Special Instructions to Applicants: • A cover letter outlining interest in the position and qualifications, including experience leading enrollment and/or marketing strategy. • An updated curriculum vitae or résumé. • Contact information for three professional references, including title, institutional affiliation, email address, and telephone number. References will not be contacted without the candidate’s written permission. The search will remain open until the position is filled. Include the official application link, salary range, employment category, location/work arrangement, and equal-opportunity statement before publication. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. The University does not provide work visa sponsorship for this position. Closing Statement: Informed by its Catholic and Marianist mission, the University is committed to the dignity of every human being. Informed by this commitment, we seek to increase diversity in all of its forms, achieve fair outcomes, and model inclusion across our campus community. The University is committed to policies of affirmative action designed to increase the employment opportunities of individuals with disabilities and protected veterans in compliance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act of 1973. Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/875/cw/en-us/job/503901/full-service-operations-supervisor": {
      "title": "Full Service Operations Supervisor",
      "description": "Full Service Operations Supervisor Apply now Job No: 503901 Work Type: Staff Full Time (1500 hours or greater) Location: Dayton, OH Category: University Staff Department: Dining Serv - VWK - 800611 Pay Grade: 9 - Non Exempt Advertised: September 23, 2026 Applications close: Position Summary: Join the University of Dayton Dining Services team and take on a leadership role where you can make a difference every day. This position provides hands-on leadership of daily dining operations, supervising staff, supporting food preparation and service across multiple platforms, and ensuring high standards of quality, sanitation, safety, and customer service. Enjoy the opportunity to grow your career while working in a supportive university environment with excellent benefits and the chance to be part of a community that values its employees. Apply to our Full Service Operations Supervisor opening today! Under the direction of the Operations Assistant, responsible for supervision of daily operation of up to 20 bargaining unit employees, 10 part-time employees and over 100 student employees within the Dining Services food service establishment. Must have working knowledge of the equipment and the food preparation processes for all of the various platforms which include but not limited to, specialized work area, Mongolian grill, Impinger ovens, convection ovens, tilt skillet, fryer, industrial dish machine, trayvayors, wood stone pizza ovens, steam tables, flat top grills, slicers, combi-ovens, steamers, turbo chef ovens and Micros cash registers. Responsibilities include but are not limited to, maintaining or improving standards of quality, service, and sanitation, supervising staff, practicing good public relations, supporting departmental objectives, maintaining security control, and performing other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: *High school graduate or equivalency. *Managerial ServSafe certified (or within one year of hire). *Two (2) years supervisory experience in food service or three (3) years of successful work experience in a restaurant or university food service operation. *Demonstrated supervisory and administrative abilities. *Ability to work with people at all levels using effective communication skills in English. *Must have a good knowledge of food preparation and sanitation. *Working knowledge of usual and customary institutional kitchen equipment and processes. *Must have a working knowledge of the internet and Microsoft Office. *Must have math skills to determine portion sizes and production needs. *Must possess the ability to work independently, supervise and direct others, without constant supervision. *Must have strong interpersonal skills. *Must be able to bend, stoop, and stand for four (4) hours at at time. *Must be able to visually differentiate colors for the purposes of food safety. *Must be able to exert fast-paced mobility. *Must be able to lift up to 40 pounds repetitively as needed. 60 pounds for Central Production. *Must be able to work in wet, cold and hot conditions usually found in a kitchen operations. Preferred Qualifications: While not everyone may possess all of the preferred qualifications, the ideal candidate will bring many of the following: *Work experience with Cbord. *Experience with food production using food processing equipment including, but not limited to, fryers, grills, slicers, steamers, combi ovens, woks, and choppers in a high volume institution such as a university, hospital, hotel or high volume restaurant. *Experience in a union workplace. *Working knowledge of cash register operations. *Associates degree in culinary, business or restaurant and hospitality management. *Valid driver’s license with low risk driving record. *Ability to be adaptable and decisive. *Ability to demonstrate integrity and strong interpersonal and organizational skills. *Demonstrates professional demeanor. *Experience working with students and a diverse, multi cultural staff. Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply please submit a cover letter addressing each minimum qualification and any applicable preferred qualifications that you meet. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. The University does not provide work visa sponsorship for this position. Closing Statement: Informed by its Catholic and Marianist mission, the University is committed to the dignity of every human being. Informed by this commitment, we seek to increase diversity in all of its forms, achieve fair outcomes, and model inclusion across our campus community. The University is committed to policies of affirmative action designed to increase the employment opportunities of individuals with disabilities and protected veterans in compliance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act of 1973. Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/875/cw/en-us/job/503905/shop-worker": {
      "title": "Shop Worker",
      "description": "Shop Worker Apply now Job No: 503905 Work Type: Staff Full Time (1500 hours or greater) Location: Dayton, OH Category: Bargaining Unit, AFSCME Department: Dining Serv - Marycrest - 800612 Pay Grade: 2 - Non Exempt Advertised: September 23, 2026 Applications close: Position Summary: Performs a variety of duties required to operate the service platforms in the Dining Services operations in a timely and efficient manner, including but not limited to; greeting and serving customers, processing meal cards and/or other cash register transactions, processing GET orders, and preparing and stocking needed supplies for all of the food court operations. Responsible for maintaining a clean, organized and neat work station, stocked as appropriate for the operation, and set up/tear down for the next meal/day operation. Responsible for the preparation of all designated areas as assigned, including but not limited to slicing, cooking and knowledge of operation of all equipment. Must follow all food handing, safety and sanitation policies and procedures. May be assigned to various or specific areas based on operational needs. Minimum Qualifications: *Must have a High School diploma or equivalency. *Must be able to effectively write and communicate in English. *Must have basic math skills. *Must be able to exert well paced mobility for periods of up to four (4) hours. *Must have the ability to lift equipment and supplies up to 40 pounds in weight. *Must be able to walk, bend, stoop, and use finger dexterity for periods up to 4 hours at a time. *Must be able to stand for up to four (4) hours at a time. *Must be able to visually differentiate colors for the purposes of food safety. *Must be able to work when exposed to wet floors, temperature extremes and loud noise. *Must be able to work independently with the appropriate amount of supervision. *Must be able to listen attentively and comprehend verbal instructions in English. Preferred Qualifications: While not everyone may possess all of the preferred qualifications, the ideal candidate will bring many of the following: *One year in a food preparation position. *Experience in a high volume a la carte operation and proven customer service skills. *Successful cash register experience. *Experience with MICROS registers. *Working knowledge of standard commercial kitchen equipment. *Current managerial ServSafe certification. *Demonstrates a professional demeanor. *Successful experience assisting customers *Experience working with students and a diverse multi cultural staff.* Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. The University does not provide work visa sponsorship for this position. This position available in multiple locations. Closing Statement: Informed by its Catholic and Marianist mission, the University is committed to the dignity of every human being. Informed by this commitment, we seek to increase diversity in all of its forms, achieve fair outcomes, and model inclusion across our campus community. The University is committed to policies of affirmative action designed to increase the employment opportunities of individuals with disabilities and protected veterans in compliance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act of 1973. Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
