    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/875/cw/en-us/job/503871/regional-enrollment-manager-ny": {
      "title": "Regional Enrollment Manager - NY",
      "description": "Regional Enrollment Manager - NY Apply now Job No: 503871 Work Type: Staff Full Time (1500 hours or greater) Location: Remote Category: University Staff Department: Recruitment & Admissions - 202500 Pay Grade: B - Exempt Advertised: September 16, 2026 Applications close: Position Summary: The University of Dayton is seeking a dynamic, energetic, and innovative Regional Enrollment Manager who is passionate about guiding students and families in the college search process. This position will report to the Senior Associate Director of Recruitment and Admission, and is expected to be based in a home office, preferably in Long Island, with travel to Long Island, New York City, Connecticut, New Hampshire, and Boston, Massachusetts. Other recruitment territories would include Vermont, Rhode Island and Maine. The Regional Enrollment Manager will work collaboratively to build upon a strong presence and recognition in recruitment territories to expand brand recognition and recruit students to the University of Dayton. Evidence-based practices will lead to intentional, strategic efforts to maximize impact within the territory. This position will manage an assigned territory through high school visits, alumni engagement, college fair representation, hosting timely and relevant event experiences, and individual appointments with students, families, and school counselors. The Regional Enrollment Manager will advise students and families through the admission and financial aid process. A successful individual will approach their work with creativity, developing innovative solutions that increase understanding of the value of a University of Dayton experience. This individual will collaborate closely with the Office of Recruitment and Admission staff to respond to questions and needs of students, parents, and other external constituents. The successful individual will have experience fostering strong relationships with diverse audiences and evidence of strong customer service, communication, and organization. Professional responsibilities include timely follow-up with students and families, external partners within the territory, and support for the Office of Recruitment and Admission through staff scheduling of phone calls, emails, virtual appointments, and some marquee on-campus events. This position will manage the coordination and execution of up to 4 regionally based events each recruitment cycle for strategic audiences, including counselors, parents, and admitted students. At the University of Dayton, a Catholic, Marianist University, we believe that diversity and inclusion are essential to the success of students and staff, and to the advancement of our educational mission. All employees are empowered to attend workshops, seminars, and other educational experiences to deepen their understanding of our mission, and each staff member is expected to meet with their supervisor semiannually to identify how they are working, individually and collaboratively, to advance the University of Dayton's educational mission. Minimum Qualifications: -Bachelor's degree. -At least 2 years of experience in college admissions, financial aid, or student services. -Commitment to contribute to an inclusive climate that includes working with students, families and external stakeholders from various backgrounds. -Effective written and verbal communication skills. -Effective public speaking. -Relationship management skills with diverse audiences. -Ability to work independently and be self-motivated. -Valid driver's license with low risk driving record. Preferred Qualifications: While not everyone may possess all of the preferred qualifications, the ideal candidate will bring many of the following: -Master's degree. -4 or more years of experience in college admission, financial aid, and/or student services at the high school or college level. -Knowledge and sensitivity to Catholic and Marianist principles of education and values. -Experience with common student enrollment systems/relational databases, such as Banner and Salesforce. Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply please submit a cover letter addressing each minimum qualification and any applicable preferred qualifications that you meet. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. The University does not provide work visa sponsorship for this position. Closing Statement: Informed by its Catholic and Marianist mission, the University is committed to the dignity of every human being. Informed by this commitment, we seek to increase diversity in all of its forms, achieve fair outcomes, and model inclusion across our campus community. The University is committed to policies of affirmative action designed to increase the employment opportunities of individuals with disabilities and protected veterans in compliance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act of 1973. Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
