    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/875/cw/en-us/job/503844/dining-service-attendant": {
      "title": "Dining Service Attendant",
      "description": "Dining Service Attendant Apply now Job No: 503844 Work Type: Staff Full Time (1500 hours or greater) Location: Dayton, OH Category: Bargaining Unit, AFSCME Department: Dining Serv - Kennedy Union - 800613 Pay Grade: 1 - Non Exempt (BU Dining) Advertised: September 02, 2026 Applications close: Position Summary: Performs a variety of duties related to food service and sanitation in a timely and efficient manner including but not limited to; greeting and serving customers, stocking counters and serving areas, preparing and replenishing beverages and food items, washing and storing properly all dishes, trays, eating utensils, cups, pots and pans. Maintains work station, other food service areas and equipment to meet cleanliness and food safety standards. Assist with preparation of items used in recipes. Assist others as directed. Must be able to effectively communicate (written and spoken) directly with other employees and staff members in English in a pleasant and professional manner. May be assigned to various or specifics areas based on operational needs. May assist with processing GET orders (Reads tickets to add condiments, beverages, desserts to order, plastic wear, takes order to appropriate pick up area.) Minimum Qualifications: *Must have a High School diploma or equivalency. *Must be able to read, write and communicate effectively in English. * Must be able to exert well paced mobility for periods of up to four (4) hours. *Must have the ability to lift equipment and supplies up to 40 pounds in weight. *Must be able to walk, bend, stoop, and use finger dexterity for periods up to four (4) hours at a time. *Must be able to stand for up to four (4) hours at a time. *Must be able to listen attentively and comprehend verbal instructions in English. *Must be able to visually differentiate colors for the purposes of food safety. *Must be able to work when exposed to wet floors, temperature extremes and loud noise. *Must be able to work independently with the appropriate amount of supervision. Preferred Qualifications: While not everyone may possess all of the preferred qualifications, the ideal candidate will bring many of the following: *Six months of experience working in food service. *Demonstrates a professional demeanor. *Successful experience assisting customers *Experience working with students and a diverse multi cultural staff and customers. Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply please submit a cover letter addressing each minimum qualification and any applicable preferred qualifications that you meet. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. The University does not provide work visa sponsorship for this position. 35 hours per week. SWING SHIFT based on operational needs. Primary 1:30pm-9:00pm-KU, 3:15p-10:45p-VWK. Must be able to work weekends and holidays. Schedule may vary for special events. Closing Statement: Informed by its Catholic and Marianist mission, the University is committed to the dignity of every human being. Informed by this commitment, we seek to increase diversity in all of its forms, achieve fair outcomes, and model inclusion across our campus community. The University is committed to policies of affirmative action designed to increase the employment opportunities of individuals with disabilities and protected veterans in compliance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act of 1973. Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
