    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/875/cw/en-us/job/503839/director-counseling-center": {
      "title": "Director, Counseling Center",
      "description": "Director, Counseling Center Job No: 503839 Work Type: Staff Full Time (1500 hours or greater) Location: Dayton, OH Category: University Staff Department: Counseling Center - 700950 Pay Grade: C - Exempt Advertised: August 31, 2026 Applications close: Position Summary: The University of Dayton, a comprehensive Catholic university in the Marianist tradition, invites applications for the position of Director, Counseling Center. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President for Student Health and Wellbeing, and serving as a member of the Student Development Leadership Team and the Health and Wellbeing Team, the Director of the Counseling Center is responsible for general oversight of an IACS accredited college counseling center and training site for burgeoning practitioners. The University seeks a visionary, innovative, and collaborative leader and strong clinician to lead the Counseling Center which is located within the new Health and Wellbeing Center. To view the position profile, please visit: keelingassociates.com and select ‘Open Searches’. The University of Dayton is seeking a visionary, innovative, and collaborative leader and strong clinician to serve as the Director, Counseling Center within the new Health and Wellbeing Center, opening in fall 2026. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President, Student Health and Wellbeing, and serving as a member of the Student Development Leadership Team and the Health and Wellbeing Team, the Director of the Counseling Center is responsible for general oversight within an IACS accredited college counseling center and training site for burgeoning practitioners. Through a hybrid care model of prevention, education, treatment, and crisis care, the Counseling Center’s mission is to provide a positive impact on the mental health, wellbeing, and academic success of all students through services that promote resiliency and capacity building and facilitate optimal student development and growth. This position is responsible for the assessment of counseling staff clinical competencies, evaluating intake and other protocols, ensuring appropriate treatment planning and documentation, providing crisis intervention and management, expanding outreach initiatives, and developing a strong referral network. The ideal candidate will provide leadership and articulate an aspirational vision for the Center; the ideal candidate will also have experience and strong skills in financial management, policy formation, assessment, and strategic planning to enhance the delivery of comprehensive mental health initiatives, psychological services, substance misuse intervention and treatment services, and collegiate recovery initiatives. The successful candidate must be dedicated to reducing barriers to care that exist for students of color, LGBTQ students, and students from other marginalized groups. The new Director will exemplify excellence in the delivery of mental health services and support the professional growth of personnel. The Director will cultivate a culture of innovation that incorporates new ideas, modalities, and operational models that address the growth in demand and increasing complexity of students’ mental health needs. Further, the Director will be called upon to regularly inform University leadership on mental health issues that affect University of Dayton students in an environment that embodies Catholic Marianist values, is primarily residential, and encompasses traditional age students. The Director will develop a broad institutional perspective and work collaboratively with other departments and campus partners. Minimum Qualifications: Candidate must meet the following minimum qualifications: • Masters degree in counseling, psychology, social work, clinical mental health or related field; • Must have or obtain Ohio licensure within six months of start date and maintain license throughout duration of employment; • Seven years of relevant and progressive professional clinical experience in administering mental health services; • Expert knowledge of the mental health needs and concerns of young adults; • Active experience in crisis intervention and emergency management operations; • Minimum two years of experience supervising professional staff; • Demonstrated experience working collaboratively with various constituents; • Articulated passion for promoting holistic wellbeing and enhancing student learning; • Experience with a multifaceted budget, including general financial management and accountability, database systems, and spreadsheets; • Demonstrated ability to manage multiple initiatives, programs, and responsibilities while ensuring clinical excellence in the provision of direct services; • Demonstrated integrity, dependability, sound judgment, teambuilding, and resourcefulness to establish and maintain collaborative, positive, and effective working relationships with multiple constituency groups; • Ability to thrive in an environment that values high expectations, accountability, service in leadership, and balanced lifestyles, while possessing exceptional verbal communication skills, enthusiasm, positive attitude, and being a self-starter with the ability to instill the same in others. • Proven success working with a range of culturally and ethnically diverse populations, and evidence of commitment to fostering equity, inclusion, and a collaborative multicultural environment; • Excellent written, oral, and digital communication skills; and • Ability to work on an on-call basis as a part of a 24/7 crisis response system that may require the person to respond to campus or a hospital/mental health facility after hours. Preferred Qualifications: While not everyone may possess all of the preferred qualifications, the ideal candidate will bring many of the following: • PhD or PsyD in counseling, psychology or related field; • Experience administering mental health services including crisis intervention and emergency management in a university setting; • Four years of successful supervisory experience in a clinical setting with knowledge of best practices in staff development, group dynamics and leading organizational change; • Demonstrated experience in developing and implementing strategic plans; • Demonstrated analytical skills to identify problems, assess alternatives, and render consistent, logical decisions; • Ability to write concise, logical, and persuasive reports; • Capacity to independently manage a variety of tasks with frequent interruptions and shifting priorities; and • Demonstrated experience with Microsoft Suite and EMR systems. Special Instructions to Applicants: The University of Dayton has partnered with Keeling & Associates in this search process. Interested candidates should send a cover letter and resume/CV, preferably in PDF format, to recruiting@ keelingassociates.com . The subject line of the email should read “University of Dayton – Director, Counseling Center.” Confidential inquiries and nominations should be addressed to Jennifer Dickson at recruiting@ keelingassociates.com . Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. The University does not provide work visa sponsorship for this position. Closing Statement: Informed by its Catholic and Marianist mission, the University is committed to the dignity of every human being. Informed by this commitment, we seek to increase diversity in all of its forms, achieve fair outcomes, and model inclusion across our campus community. The University is committed to policies of affirmative action designed to increase the employment opportunities of individuals with disabilities and protected veterans in compliance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act of 1973. Back to search results Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/875/cw/en-us/job/503821/catering-event-supervisor": {
      "title": "Catering Event Supervisor",
      "description": "Catering Event Supervisor Apply now Job No: 503821 Work Type: Staff Full Time (1500 hours or greater) Location: Dayton, OH Category: University Staff Department: Dining Serv - Catering - 800618 Pay Grade: 9 - Non Exempt Advertised: August 27, 2026 Applications close: Position Summary: Join the University of Dayton Catering team and play a key role in bringing exceptional events to life! Lead and support catering staff, coordinate event details, and ensure every guest experience reflects UD’s commitment to outstanding service, teamwork, and excellence. Apply to our Catering Event Supervisor opening today! Under direction of the Catering Services Operations Assistant and Catering General Manager, the Event Supervisor oversees catering staff at various locations. The Event Supervisor is responsible for execution of events according to guest specifications as listed on service orders. The Event Supervisor also oversees set up, delivery, service, and inventory, and ensures all safety and sanitation procedures are being properly followed. Responsibilities also include supervising retail operations for bar and other food service venues under the Catering department. Minimum Qualifications: *Must have high school diploma or equivalent. *Must have minimum of three (3) years of experience in a food prep and/or food service position. *Must have working knowledge of commercial kitchen equipment. *Must have experience supervising and training personnel in proper food service techniques. *Must possess the ability to work independently and supervise others without direct supervision. *Must have the proven ability to be a self starter. Must have the proven ability to demonstrate creativity. *Must have proven ability to work with people at all levels in a professional, friendly, and helpful manner. *Must have the ability to manage numerous details in a multiple priority and fast paced environment. *Must be able to write and communicate effectively in English. *Must be well organized and attentive to detail. Must be able to exert fast paced mobility. *Must be able to bend, stoop and stand for four (4) hours at a time. *Must be able to visually differentiate colors for the purpose of food safety. *Must be able to lift up to 75 lbs. and do occasional heavy physical labor. *Must have a valid driver's license with less than six (6) points and certifiable per University requirements. *Must be able to drive catering transport vehicles. *Must be able to work nights and weekends and adapt to a flexible schedule. *Must possess certification in Managerial ServSafe (or within 1 year of hire). Preferred Qualifications: While not everyone may possess all of the preferred qualifications, the ideal candidate will bring many of the following: *Associate Degree in Culinary Arts, Business or Hospitality Management. *Previous successful catering supervisory experience. *Demonstrated experience working in a multi event/facility or environment. *Current Managerial ServSafe certification. *Demonstrated professional demeanor. Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply please submit a cover letter addressing each minimum qualification and any applicable preferred qualifications that you meet. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. The University does not provide work visa sponsorship for this position. Closing Statement: Informed by its Catholic and Marianist mission, the University is committed to the dignity of every human being. Informed by this commitment, we seek to increase diversity in all of its forms, achieve fair outcomes, and model inclusion across our campus community. The University is committed to policies of affirmative action designed to increase the employment opportunities of individuals with disabilities and protected veterans in compliance with the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and Vietnam Era Veterans' Readjustment Assistance Act of 1973. Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
